<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wat Phra That Hariphunchai</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wat Phra That Hariphunchai is a Buddhist temple in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lamphun">Lamphun</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, centred on a gilded stupa said to enshrine a relic of the Buddha. Tradition credits its founding to King Adityaraja of the Mon kingdom of Hariphunchai. It is one of the most important pilgrimage sites of the former kingdom of Lan Na.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wat-phra-that-hariphunchai.jpg" alt="Wat Phra That Hariphunchai" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This Photo was taken by Supanut Arunoprayote. Feel free to use any of my images, but please mention me as the author ... · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wat_Phra_That_Hariphunchai_(III).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
